{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SBbBiX66iq4MyxRuVDfnuc","type":"tool_result","content":"# Farmers Markets Data Summary\n\n**All Rows (CSV Format):**\nThe data contains 53 entries spanning U.S. states, D.C., and territories, with columns for state name, abbreviation, farmers markets, CSA programs, farm stands, SNAP/EBT acceptance, organic vendors, and website availability.\n\n**Total Farmers Markets (50 States + D.C.):**\n**9,271 farmers markets**\n\nThis sum excludes Puerto Rico (2) and the Virgin Islands (0), counting only the 50 states and the District of Columbia as requested.\n\nThe data shows California leads with 647 markets, followed by New York with 555 and Pennsylvania with 426 farmers markets."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca15557f-ed6e-46f1-89d7-41970366004c","uuid":"58af630d-7bc1-4c78-9f86-9f8c8f8d80f4","timestamp":"2026-08-16T20:09:19.512Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":2651,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Farmers Markets Data Summary\n\n**All Rows (CSV Format):**\nThe data contains 53 entries spanning U.S. states, D.C., and territories, with columns for state name, abbreviation, farmers markets, CSA programs, farm stands, SNAP/EBT acceptance, organic vendors, and website availability.\n\n**Total Farmers Markets (50 States + D.C.):**\n**9,271 farmers markets**\n\nThis sum excludes Puerto Rico (2) and the Virgin Islands (0), counting only the 50 states and the District of Columbia as requested.\n\nThe data shows California leads with 647 markets, followed by New York with 555 and Pennsylvania with 426 farmers markets.","durationMs":2579,"url":"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv"}}
